# Nine stations in series from Dai, Nguyen & Reiman (1994), Section 3.3
# Deterministic arrivals (ca^2_{a,1} = 0), exponential service (cs^2 = 1)
# rho_i = 0.6 for 1 <= i <= 8, rho_9 = 0.9
# Customers arrive at station 1, proceed 1->2->...->9->exit
# Service rates: mu_i = 1/tau_i, with lambda = alpha_1 (the arrival rate)
# Since all lambda_i = alpha (tandem), and rho_i = alpha * tau_i:
#   For rho_i = 0.6: tau_i = 0.6/alpha
#   For rho_9 = 0.9: tau_9 = 0.9/alpha
# Choose alpha = 1.0, then tau_i = 0.6 for i=1..8, tau_9 = 0.9
# Natural partition: S1 = {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8}, S2 = {9}
# Expected total waiting time: 10.06 (SBD), 10.05 (sim) from Table VIII
9
